  ### Key Issues Found & Fixed
                                                                                  
  #### 1. Scanner Script Syntax Error & Shell Injection
  (radar_prototype.sh:112-245)                                                    

  • Bug: In perform_scan, $scan_output from termux-wifi-scaninfo was
  interpolated directly into a single-quoted Python string inside python3 -c
  "process_scan_data('$scan_output')". Because scan output contains formatted
  multiline JSON and SSIDs frequently contain single quotes (e.g. "Ash's
  House"), Python immediately aborted with SyntaxError: unterminated string
  literal.
  • Fix: Rewrote data ingestion to pass scan JSON securely through sys.stdin
  (json.load(sys.stdin)).
  • Field Compatibility: Real termux-wifi-scaninfo output uses frequency_mhz
  and rssi (not frequency and level). The parser now handles both Termux native
  keys and sample JSON keys.
  • CLI Support: Added radar_prototype.sh once for one-shot scans.

  #### 2. Distance Model 1,000x Calculation Error (radar_prototype.sh:173-186)

  • Bug: The previous Free Space Path Loss (FSPL) distance formula used +32.45
  (which expects distance in kilometers) while treating the output as meters,
  resulting in calculated distances that were 1, 000 × too small (all signals
  collapsed between 0.10 m and 3.14 m).
  • Fix: Replaced with an indoor log-distance path loss propagation model (RSSI
  = -30 - 10 · n · log₁₀(d) with n = 2.8), yielding accurate real-world
  distances:
      • Strong nearby signal (-40 dBm) →≈ 2.3 m
      • Room level (-55 dBm) →≈ 7.8 m
      • Neighbor / corridor (-75 dBm) →≈ 40.5 m
      • Distant network (-90 dBm) →≈ 138.9 m


  #### 3. Inverted Radar Positioning & Hash Randomization (app.py:137-163)
                                                                                  
  • Bug: The radius calculation radius = (1 - normalized_distance) * 0.8
  inverted the radar: strong/close signals were placed at the outer boundary,
  while weak/distant signals were placed at the center observer dot.
  • Fix: Corrected radius formula so closer devices are near the center and
  distant devices radiate outward to the perimeter rings (r ∈ [0.12, 0.88]).
  • Stability: Replaced Python's randomized hash(bssid) with deterministic MD5
  hashing so device angles and Google Earth KML placemarks stay consistent
  across server restarts.
                                                                                  
  #### 4. Wi-Fi Band Anomaly Penalties (risk_engine.py:220-245)

  • Bug: The risk engine only allowed 2.4 GHz channels. Every modern 5 GHz        
  (5150–5900 MHz) and Wi-Fi 6E/7 (5925–7125 MHz) network was automatically
  penalized with +25 points as an "unusual channel anomaly".
  • Fix: Updated frequency verification to recognize all standardized 2.4 GHz,    
  5 GHz, and 6 GHz Wi-Fi bands, added WPA3/SAE capability recognition, and
  guarded against None values in capabilities and signal levels.                  

  #### 5. Missing Routes & UI Exception Handling

  • Missing /demo Route: start_mobile.sh and docs pointed to
  http://localhost:5000/demo, which returned 404. Added the /demo route to
